---
const SIGNUP_URL = 'https://go.marginapp.in';
const periods = ['Since inception', 'Last 12 months', 'Last 3 years', 'CY 2025', 'FY 2025-26'];
const tags = ['Since inception', 'Trailing', 'Calendar year', 'Financial year', 'Per stock', 'Per list', 'Full portfolio'];
---

<section class="py-24 lg:py-32 overflow-hidden bg-navy-800/20">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-16 items-center">

      <div class="reveal order-2 lg:order-1">
        <div class="relative rounded-xl border border-border bg-navy-800/60 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-gold-400/30 to-transparent"></div>
          <div class="p-6">
            <p class="text-xs text-muted tracking-widest uppercase mb-4">Returns &amp; Tax Summary</p>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5 mb-6">
              {periods.map((period, i) => (
                <span class={`px-2.5 py-1 text-[11px] rounded-full border ${i === 4 ? 'text-gold-300 border-gold-400/40 bg-gold-400/5' : 'text-muted border-border'}`}>
                  {period}
                </span>
              ))}
            </div>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 mb-4">
              {[
                { label: 'XIRR (annualised)', value: '21.3%', positive: true },
                { label: 'Absolute return', value: '18.6%', positive: true },
                { label: 'Opening value', value: '₹18.2L' },
                { label: 'Closing value', value: '₹24.1L' },
              ].map((stat) => (
                <div class="rounded-lg bg-navy-950/50 border border-border/60 p-4">
                  <p class="text-xs text-muted mb-1">{stat.label}</p>
                  <p class={`font-display text-2xl font-semibold ${stat.positive ? 'text-emerald-400' : 'text-cream'}`}>
                    {stat.value}
                  </p>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-lg bg-navy-950/50 border border-border/60 p-4 mb-4">
              <p class="text-xs text-muted mb-3">Gain breakdown, current FY</p>
              <div class="space-y-2">
                {[
                  { label: 'Short-term, 20%', pct: 40, color: 'bg-amber-400' },
                  { label: 'Long-term, 12.5%', pct: 60, color: 'bg-emerald-500' },
                ].map((row) => (
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                    <div class="flex-1 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-navy-700 overflow-hidden">
                      <div class={`h-full rounded-full ${row.color}`} style={`width: ${row.pct}%`}></div>
                    </div>
                    <span class="text-xs text-muted w-36 shrink-0">{row.label} · {row.pct}%</span>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-start gap-2 text-xs text-muted">
              <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-amber-400 mt-1 shrink-0"></span>
              <span>CY 2019 has no closing price at the period start, so it reports no rate rather than a wrong one.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal reveal-delay-2 order-1 lg:order-2">
        <p class="text-xs text-gold-400 tracking-widest uppercase mb-4">Returns &amp; Tax</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-light text-cream leading-tight mb-6">
          Your returns, your tax,<br />
          <em class="font-semibold not-italic">period by period</em>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">
          XIRR accounts for every buy, sell and dividend on the date it happened. Margin runs it over
          the period you pick: since inception, a trailing stretch of 1, 2, 3 or 5 years, a calendar
          year, or a financial year. Ask it of one stock, of any list, or of the whole portfolio,
          alongside the absolute return, the gain, and the opening and closing value of the period.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Where a period cannot yield a rate, Margin says which period and why: nothing was held or
          traded, there is no closing price on the period start to value the opening position, or the
          cash flows never turn around inside the period. It reports no number in place of a number
          it cannot stand behind.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed mb-8">
          On sales it separates short-term from long-term capital gains and applies the rate in force
          on the date of the sale: 20% and 12.5% from April 2024, and 15% and 10% for gains realised
          before that.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-8">
          {tags.map((tag) => (
            <span class="px-3 py-1 text-xs text-muted border border-border rounded-full">{tag}</span>
          ))}
        </div>
        <a
          href={SIGNUP_URL}
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-gold-400 hover:text-gold-300 transition-colors group"
        >
          See your real returns
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13.5 4.5 21 12m0 0-7.5 7.5M21 12H3" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
